### Message struct definition

Source: https://github.com/axllent/mailpit/blob/develop/_autodocs/types.md

Defines the Message struct used for storing and returning message data. It includes fields for headers, body, attachments, and metadata. Produced by storage.GetMessage(id) and JSON-encoded by GET /api/v1/message/{id}.

```go
// Message data excluding physical attachments
//
// swagger:model Message
type Message struct {
	// Database ID
	ID string
	// Message ID
	MessageID string
	// From address
	From *mail.Address
	// To addresses
	To []*mail.Address
	// Cc addresses
	Cc []*mail.Address
	// Bcc addresses
	Bcc []*mail.Address
	// ReplyTo addresses
	ReplyTo []*mail.Address
	// Return-Path
	ReturnPath string
	// Message subject
	Subject string
	// List-Unsubscribe header information
	ListUnsubscribe ListUnsubscribe
	// Message RFC3339Nano date & time (if set), else date & time received
	Date time.Time
	// Message tags
	Tags []string
	// Username used for authentication (if provided) with the SMTP or Send API
	Username string
	// Message body text
	Text string
	// Message body HTML
	HTML string
	// Message size in bytes
	Size uint64
	// Inline message attachments
	Inline []Attachment
	// Message attachments
	Attachments []Attachment
}
```

--------------------------------

### Send a message via Mailpit API

Source: https://github.com/axllent/mailpit/blob/develop/_autodocs/api-reference/apiv1.md

Use this snippet to send a new message through the Mailpit API. The request is a POST to /api/v1/send with a JSON body containing sender, recipient, subject, and text. The response includes the message ID.

```bash
curl -s -X POST http://localhost:8025/api/v1/send \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"From":{"Name":"John","Email":"john@example.com"},
       "To":[{"Email":"jane@example.com"}],
       "Subject":"Hi","Text":"Hello!"}'
# → {"ID":"iAfZVVe2UQfNSG5BAjgYwa"}
```

### Mailpit — Types > Message

Source: https://github.com/axllent/mailpit/blob/develop/_autodocs/types.md

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `ID` | `string` | ✓ | Database ID (22-char shortuuid) |
| `MessageID` | `string` | ✓ | RFC Message-ID header (angle brackets stripped) |
| `From` | `*mail.Address` | ✓ | Sender |
| `To`/`Cc`/`Bcc`/`ReplyTo` | `[]*mail.Address` | ✓ | Recipients |
| `ReturnPath` | `string` | ✓ | From Return-Path header, falls back to From address |
| `Subject` | `string` | ✓ | Subject header |
| `ListUnsubscribe` | `ListUnsubscribe` | ✓ | Parsed List-Unsubscribe info |
| `Date` | `time.Time` | ✓ | Message Date (RFC3339Nano); received time if header missing |
| `Tags` | `[]string` | ✓ | Message tags |
| `Username` | `string` | ✓ | Authenticated username (SMTP/Send API) |
| `Text` | `string` | ✓ | Plain-text body |
| `HTML` | `string` | ✓ | HTML body |
| `Size` | `uint64` | ✓ | Raw size in bytes |
| `Inline` | `[]Attachment` | ✓ | Inline parts (CID images) |
| `Attachments` | `[]Attachment` | ✓ | Attachments |

Produced by `storage.GetMessage(id) (*Message, error)`; JSON-encoded by `GET /api/v1/message/{id}`. Exported alias `apiv1.Message`.

